    "available_at": "2026-11-17T18:56:35.118742+00:00",
    "body": "Volkswagen will reveal the new GTI hot hatch on Friday, promising it will be “something really spicy.”\nVolkswagen is launching a spicy new EV hot hatch\nTo celebrate the GTI’s 50th anniversary, Volkswagen is “starting a new chapter,” with its first all-electric model to bear the iconic performance badge.\nThe ID. Polo GTI “brings the legendary GTI driving pleasure into the electric future,” VW said after opening pre-orders last month.\nVolkswagen previewed a mysterious new hot hatch draped under a cloth that appears to be a souped-up version of the ID. Polo GTI. Despite its attempt to “hide” it, you can see the massive rear wing and wide wheel arches under the cloth.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nThe company promised that “something really spicy” will be served this Friday, November 20, with the tags #Volkswagen, #GTI, and #GTI50.\nAlthough no other details were revealed, the new hot hatch is thought to be the more powerful “Clubsport” variant.\nView this post on Instagram A post shared by Volkswagen (@volkswagen)\nVolkswagen’s head of driving dynamics, Florian Umbach, told Autocar earlier this year that the company is planning to launch the ID. Polo GTI Clubsport, a more powerful variant that will deliver close to 300 hp, up from 223 hp in the standard model.\nUmbach said that Volkswagen is developing “a similar kind of paddleshift power delivery that the Hyundai N cars have” for the upcoming electric hot hatch.\nVolkswagen ID. Polo GTI (Source: Volkswagen)\nHyundai’s performance EVs, the IONIQ 5 N and IONIQ 6 N, feature a simulated gear-shifting system called N e-Shift that uses paddle shifters on the steering wheel to replicate the feel of an 8-speed dual-clutch transmission. It works with the N Active Sound+ system to make it feel like you’re in a traditional gas-powered sports car.\nIt has yet to be confirmed whether the hot hatch debuting on Friday is, in fact, the new ID. Polo Clubsport, but the design clues give us a good idea of what’s coming.\nVolkswagen previews new “really spicy” GTI hot hatch (Source: Volkswagen)\nTop comment by Will Smith\nLiked by 2 people\nMan, $45k for a starting price is a little uncomfortably steep for a hatch, given there are a little bigger options in that range. I wish it started somewhere in the 30s to be competitive.\nView all comments\nCheck back on Friday for the full details.\nVolkswagen opened pre-orders for the ID. Polo GTI last month, starting at 39,995 euros (about $45,000).\nLike the first Golf GTI from 1976, the electric ID. Polo GTI uses a front-wheel-drive powertrain. The front-mounted electric motor delivers 223 hp (166 kW) and 213 lb-ft (290 Nm) of instant torque, enabling it to sprint from 0 to 62 mph (0 to 100 km/h) in 6.8 seconds.\nIn early 2027, Volkswagen will open orders for the ID.3 GTI , the second EV to wear the badge, and its first rear-wheel-drive (RWD) GTI.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
